Z||000008||bad911||03-22-2001||09:17 PM||||Thanks for the welcoming and support guys. Awesome shot of your machine, Roger, very nice. Well, I went junking today and with Firebird and Caddies both present, I ended up getting an 86 Deville with a 4.1. [My little lady will insist that I have my head examined if/when she finds out, so sshhhh!] Saw three Caddies, all 4.1's. So haste loses getting a 4.5 or 4.9. Oh well, the pistons are used anyway, might as well bore it. Originally I'd wanted to do the 3.4 for a quick-n-easy, but the deciding factor was the tranny upgrade to the 4 spd slushbox. Hope I'm not delusional in understanding that it slips right in... anybody recommend a silkscreener to do a "3" on my gear indicator? ;-D  Ya think we can make that TBI rock with the extra fuel pressure? YAH!!!  ||||reg||1
